      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. it's a lot better than the draft, but i'm worried it's still looking a bit light on the thoroughness metric. the score is sitting pretty low for a main course recipe.\n\ncan you try a version that's a bit more detailed? maybe expand the steps a little more to ensure the ingredient mentions are higher so we pass the automated check. again, please keep it sounding natural and don't just list the ingredients over and over, i just want it to feel more \"comprehensive.\"",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here's a revised version:\n\n\"To prepare this dish, start by heating a generous 12-inch pan over medium-high heat and add 2 tablespoons of unsalted butter. Once melted, sauté 1 large chopped onion, rinsed and drained to remove excess moisture, until it's softened and translucent, about 5 minutes. Next, minimize the garlic pieces to 2-3 cloves and mince them finely, then add and stir into the pan until fragrant, about 1 minute. For added richness, pour in 1 cup of heavy cream and sprinkle a pinch of salt to taste, about 1/8 teaspoon, then stir to combine with the onion and garlic mixture. As the sauce simmers over low heat, let it cook for 5-7 minutes, allowing the cream to thicken slightly and reduce the liquid. Just before serving, add 1 handful of fresh spinach leaves, chopped or torn, and cook until wilted, stirring occasionally, about 2-3 minutes. To finish, taste and adjust the seasoning with a pinch of freshly ground pepper, if desired. Finally, serve the spinach sauce over cooked pasta, tossed with a fork to coat evenly.\"",
      "source": "target",
